From 615d0c65be3741b2098f9b18976617fd4698298a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 16:57:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] ktranslate: decode topology capability bitmaps into
 readable names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the generic decodeCapabilityBits helper with two protocol-aware
decoders. decodeLLDPCapabilities walks the BITS octet string per
IEEE 802.1AB (bit 0 = MSB of byte 0) and emits names from the 8 defined
bits — other, repeater, bridge, wlan-ap, router, telephone, docsis,
station-only. decodeCDPCapabilities interprets the cdpCacheCapabilities
value as a big-endian integer and emits names from the 10 CISCO-CDP-MIB
bits — router, trans-bridge, source-route-bridge, switch, host,
igmp-conditional, repeater, phone, remotely-managed, cvta.

Both decoders fall back to a "0x…" hex token when no known bits are set,
so vendor extensions or undefined bits still survive the round trip.

Updates the existing two-neighbor tests to assert on the decoded names,
adds focused unit tests for each decoder, and refreshes the README so
the documented remote_capabilities format matches reality.
